        "original_id": "8aac483f-82e7-5330-9faf-cc9a2500600d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mariqueen Maandig Reznor, Pelle Almqvist, Trent Reznor, Atticus Ross\n- Projects: An Omen EP, Welcome Oblivion, Ice Age\n- Organizations: Nine Inch Nails, How to Destroy Angels\n- Roles: musician, singer-songwriter, singer, songwriter, producer, collaborator\n\nFacts:\n- Pelle Almqvist was born on 29 May 1978 and is a Swedish singer and songwriter also known as Howlin' Pelle Almqvist.\n- Mariqueen Maandig Reznor, née Maandig, was born on April 5, 1981 and is a Filipino American musician and singer-songwriter.\n- Trent Reznor was the frontman of Nine Inch Nails when he produced An Omen EP with Mariqueen Maandig and longtime collaborator Atticus Ross.\n- An Omen EP contained various tracks that were later issued on the 2013 debut album Welcome Oblivion.\n- Ice Age is a song by the American post-industrial group How to Destroy Angels from its second release, An Omen EP.",
